  "text": " is Jevan Souteno and I'm going to present Trust Connect. So Trust Connect is a conversation reader. Basically what we're doing is a v-con powered real-time visibility and compliance for global distributed teams. So think of it as an enterprise that has a lot of branches globally and probably from the HQ how will they be able to have really real-time visibility and how they can be able to monitor on how issues and complaints are being processed in individual branches in different countries. So Trust the conversation, connect the dots. So the global blind spot. HQ uses control where teams go distributed. So what we have is siloed branch operations. Global branches, let's say, Nairobi, Lagos, New York operate independently. HQ has zero real-time visibility without manual reports from each branch manager. Delayed pattern detection, scattered conversion data and no cross-region intelligence. So what pain points are we trying to address here? We have realized there's usually knowledge isolation, especially now if people work in the East African market, they work for whatever knowledge they have. People in the West African, people in North America, South America and that. And then also we have week-long blind spots. So something might be happening in real-time but then now it's only after weekly meeting or bi-weekly meeting as well now the HQ is being informed by the branch manager on this other progress. So we are trying to see how we can use vicon and cloud desktop. So that's the HQ can be able to monitor in real-time and get global visibility on how different patches are working and how best to escalate certain situations so that we can be able to move faster. So what the solution we are doing is we are creating a v-code-powered intelligence. So capture all conversations into standardized vicon format and then we incorporate the MCP of cloud where now AI queries. So where now you can directly query and be able to be able to understand and make sense of what 